1
00:00:00,353 --> 00:00:03,097
Staff run the event from the admin console.

2
00:00:03,097 --> 00:00:07,882
The presence map shows every table: teams that are here, a judge at a table

3
00:00:07,882 --> 00:00:11,009
projects held for review, and teams not here yet.

4
00:00:12,996 --> 00:00:15,422
The Judges tab shows each judge's pace.

5
00:00:15,422 --> 00:00:18,781
A judge rushing through tables gets a Fast visits flag

6
00:00:18,781 --> 00:00:20,460
with the numbers behind it.

7
00:00:20,462 --> 00:00:22,730
An admin can void that judge's votes.

8
00:00:22,730 --> 00:00:25,550
It needs a reason, which goes in the audit log

9
00:00:25,550 --> 00:00:28,676
and every room is ranked again without those votes.

10
00:00:28,676 --> 00:00:30,638
The row is stamped Votes voided.

11
00:00:32,342 --> 00:00:35,406
The Flagged tab is the review queue: late commits

12
00:00:35,406 --> 00:00:38,469
a teammate who isn't registered, a path mismatch.

13
00:00:38,469 --> 00:00:43,283
An admin clears a project into judging, or escalates it with a written reason

14
00:00:43,283 --> 00:00:47,222
and an escalated project stays out until the organizers decide.

15
00:00:49,599 --> 00:00:53,937
From the Overview, Print placards opens a sheet for every table

16
00:00:53,937 --> 00:00:55,383
one placard per page.

17
00:00:55,385 --> 00:00:58,131
Each sheet has its own QR code and check code.

18
00:00:58,131 --> 00:01:02,369
Judges scan it, or type the code, to prove they are at the right table.

19
00:01:03,917 --> 00:01:07,073
The Settings tab holds the event-wide switches.

20
00:01:07,073 --> 00:01:11,237
Table talk goes on, then off again, and each flip is recorded.

21
00:01:11,241 --> 00:01:13,262
That record is the audit log.

22
00:01:13,262 --> 00:01:18,139
Every switch, escalation and voided vote lands there: who did it, when

23
00:01:18,139 --> 00:01:19,881
and any reason they gave.

24
00:01:22,731 --> 00:01:27,291
That's Gav-IL: fair, fast judging for HackIllinois 2027.
